    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1450">

                <pb facs="0947" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg831"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/469.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Willard to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Minister of State requests me to inform you of contents of telegram received
                    last night from Spanish Minister, Mexico City, Bouquet: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Notwithstanding absolute guaranties repeatedly given by the chief of the
                            Zapata forces, various Spaniards have been assassinated, many houses
                            sacked and frequent robberies in the streets, there being a total
                            absence of energetic action on part of authorities which change from day
                            to day. For the moment there are no persons to whom to apply for
                            protection.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
